to back it up.

156
00:13:57.756 --> 00:14:01.352
Thank you, sir. I'll pack up
and report to the deck department--

157
00:14:01.428 --> 00:14:04.329
You're just there to swim.
Nothing else.

158
00:14:04.397 --> 00:14:06.831
Stay with the stewards.

159
00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.300
Let him out.

160
00:14:09.369 --> 00:14:12.770
Hey, Carl. You know, the only reason
your ass ain't in the brig...

161
00:14:12.839 --> 00:14:15.307
is 'cause you high yellow, boy.

162
00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:17.309
- Damn!
- Search and Rescue Squad.

163
00:14:17.377 --> 00:14:19.642
Boy, you in good
with Captain Pullman now.

164
00:14:19.714 --> 00:14:22.342
Put in a good word for me, they
might let me drive the boat.

165
00:14:22.416 --> 00:14:24.509
"You're never
gonna believe it, but yesterday...

166
00:14:24.585 --> 00:14:26.985
I made Seaman, which is Navy
for a glorified deck hand.

167
00:14:27.054 --> 00:14:30.182
I'm still not sure what I'm gonna be,
but I'll make you proud of me yet.

168
00:14:30.257 --> 00:14:33.954
Anyway, Dad, sounds like the mail
chopper's here, so I better get topside.

169
00:14:34.028 --> 00:14:37.260
Give Mom a big hug for me.
Your loving son, Carl. "

170
00:14:42.537 --> 00:14:46.633
- Good afternoon, Chief.

171
00:14:46.708 --> 00:14:48.903
What the--

172
00:14:55.002 --> 00:14:58.062
Mail chopper clipped
a radio mast!He's down!He's down!

173
00:15:02.576 --> 00:15:07.809
Splash a diver, now!Men on
that chopper. I want 'em up alive.

174
00:15:11.084 --> 00:15:13.485
Diver's coming up.

175
00:15:14.556 --> 00:15:18.219
Bring it up.
Bring it up!

176
00:15:20.562 --> 00:15:22.587
Come on! Faster! Pull him up!
Come on, Vince. Pull him up!

177
00:15:22.664 --> 00:15:26.225
- Come on! Faster, faster!
- Brashear, get on that steadying line.

178
00:15:26.301 --> 00:15:29.532
Keep it up!
Lay back into that! Keep it steady!

179
00:15:29.604 --> 00:15:32.665
Keep it steady!
Keep it steady!

180
00:15:38.848 --> 00:15:41.339
Bring him in!
Coming down!

181
00:15:45.421 --> 00:15:47.548
Bring him down!

182
00:15:49.326 --> 00:15:52.193
Sailors, get him up!
On the hatch. Ready?

183
00:15:52.262 --> 00:15:53.889
Come on.

184
00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.534
Face down!

185
00:16:18.189 --> 00:16:19.884
- No.
- Goddamn!

186
00:16:19.957 --> 00:16:23.256
If I'd just been a couple of minutes
earlier, he'd be breathin'now!

187
00:16:23.327 --> 00:16:25.262
You did your best,
Chief Sunday. Lieutenant Hanks.

188
00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.298
Sir.

189
00:16:27.366 --> 00:16:30.130
- Complete the diving operation.
- Yes, sir.

190
00:16:30.202 --> 00:16:32.261
The copilot is still in the water.

191
00:16:32.337 --> 00:16:35.500
Caughlin, it's your turn over the side.
Bring that man home. Hat him.

192
00:16:35.574 --> 00:16:38.839
Take Chief Sunday to the chamber
for decompression.

193
00:16:45.151 --> 00:16:47.813
Lay back on him.
On the side!

194
00:16:47.887 --> 00:16:50.788
Diver comin'up
and over!

195
00:17:02.536 --> 00:17:05.027
- Chief?
- Drop the goddamn weight!

196
00:17:05.105 --> 00:17:06.800
Drop the weight!

197
00:17:19.854 --> 00:17:21.845
- Man overboard!
- Stand by divers, you're in!

198
00:17:21.923 --> 00:17:23.857
What the hell's going on?

199
00:17:23.925 --> 00:17:27.190
Master Chief,
we just lost Caughlin, sir.

200
00:17:27.262 --> 00:17:30.254
- We got a standby diver going--
- He can't wait that long.

201
00:17:30.332 --> 00:17:32.596
Tellme what you're doing?
I got a man on.

202
00:17:32.667 --> 00:17:34.999
Gonna bounce dive, put him on
a rescue line and yank him out.

203
00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.040
- Bounce dive?
- Bounce back before
the nitrogen builds in my system.

204
00:17:38.107 --> 00:17:41.304
He's too deep already,
and you will call me "sir."

205
00:17:41.377 --> 00:17:43.368
Goddamn it, I got a man dyin'
down there, sir!

206
00:17:43.446 --> 00:17:47.644
Give mea wrench! Give me
that spare life line and air hose!

207
00:17:47.717 --> 00:17:49.947
I've lost two men
on my watch.

208
00:17:50.019 --> 00:17:52.544
I've got another drowning, and I'm not
about to let you commit suicide.

209
00:17:52.622 --> 00:17:55.250
- You will stand fast!
- He'll be dead before you get to him!

210
00:17:55.324 --> 00:17:58.419
- The air hose!
- Stand off! I will take you
to the captain's mast,

211
00:17:58.495 --> 00:18:01.362
and you will lose if you touch
that water, do you hear me?

212
00:18:01.431 --> 00:18:03.558
Yes, sir!

213
00:18:06.803 --> 00:18:08.896
Goddamn it!

214
00:18:28.426 --> 00:18:33.524
Master Chief Sunday,
you've sustained a serious embolism.

215
00:18:33.599 --> 00:18:37.968
- Embolism?
- Both lobes of the lungs
were severely scarred.

216
00:18:38.037 --> 00:18:40.301
Can't cheat the laws of nature
forever, can you, Doc?

217
00:18:40.372 --> 00:18:43.307
I'm afraid the condition's
totally inoperable.

218
00:18:43.375 --> 00:18:45.935
Ain't that a bitch?

219
00:18:49.281 --> 00:18:52.718
So what happens next time I go diving?
I start taking on bottom pressure?

220
00:18:52.786 --> 00:18:56.153
Any increased pressure at all
will kill you, instantly.

221
00:18:56.222 --> 00:19:00.784
Kill me. Goddamn, for a minute there
I thought this was serious.

222
00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.385
- If you could keep your voice down.
- Hell, no.

223
00:19:03.463 --> 00:19:05.761
Goddamn,
I feel like singin', man.

224
00:19:05.832 --> 00:19:09.462
- Ah, fuck!
- Where are you going?

225
00:19:09.537 --> 00:19:13.064
Get me a drink. Celebrate.
You had me going.
I thought I couldn't go diving no more.

226
00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:16.109
- Chief Sunday,
you're scaring the patients.
- How about me?

227
00:19:16.177 --> 00:19:20.238
Goddamn. Hey, I got an idea.
Maybe you can use me around here.

228
00:19:20.314 --> 00:19:23.306
Hell, I'm lookin'
to make a career move.

229
00:19:23.384 --> 00:19:27.082
Maybe, maybe you can get
someone to change the bed pans!

230
00:19:27.155 --> 00:19:30.989
- Change the fuckin' bed pans!
- Chief!

231
00:19:31.059 --> 00:19:33.789
- Change the fuckin' bed pans!
Hey! Hey!
- Hey!

232
00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:42.434
Master Chief Sunday, given
your current physical condition...

233
00:19:42.504 --> 00:19:46.771
and the far graver issue...

234
00:19:46.843 --> 00:19:49.004
