disqualified from diving,

236
00:19:52.181 --> 00:19:54.706
fined one-half month's pay
for three months...

237
00:19:54.784 --> 00:19:57.048
and reassigned
toa training position,

238
00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:59.850
where it is
my greatest wish...

239
00:19:59.922 --> 00:20:03.222
that you will embrace
a new found respect for authority.

240
00:20:07.264 --> 00:20:09.198
This hearing is concluded.

241
00:20:43.102 --> 00:20:46.765
- That's what I want to be, sir.
- A Navy Master Diver?

242
00:20:46.839 --> 00:20:50.104
- Yes, sir.
- Last week, you were a cook.

243
00:20:50.176 --> 00:20:54.840
- Well, the man I just saw--
- The man you saw is a Master Chief.

244
00:20:54.914 --> 00:20:57.748
That's the highest rank an enlisted man
can achieve in the Navy.

245
00:20:57.818 --> 00:21:01.413
A lot of good men spend a career
trying to get there and fail.

246
00:21:01.488 --> 00:21:04.082
Besides,

247
00:21:04.157 --> 00:21:06.682
they are not gonna take
a colored at diving school.

248
00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:11.254
- It's as simple as that.
- What if you were to give me
a personal recommendation, sir?

249
00:21:11.331 --> 00:21:16.269
I just made you
a deck seaman three days ago.

250
00:21:16.337 --> 00:21:19.135
What else do I owe you?

251
00:21:19.207 --> 00:21:23.644
The way I see it,
I owe you, sir.

252
00:21:31.185 --> 00:21:34.451
I'll endorse your request,

253
00:21:34.523 --> 00:21:36.957
but it ain't gonna work.

254
00:22:12.413 --> 00:22:14.176
Wait outside.

255
00:22:22.156 --> 00:22:27.595
- Mr. Pappy, Boats wain's Mate
Bras hear is reporting for duty.
- Don't let him in, sailor.

256
00:22:36.004 --> 00:22:39.462
I'll be waiting on the hilltop

257
00:22:39.541 --> 00:22:43.477
Where the wild
red roses grow

258
00:22:43.545 --> 00:22:48.108
Yeah. Well, look at Mr. Navy.

259
00:22:48.184 --> 00:22:50.812
Bell-bottoms bleached.

260
00:22:50.887 --> 00:22:52.878
Shoes all shined up.

261
00:22:52.955 --> 00:22:55.219
Now alls we need
is an organ grinder.

262
00:22:55.291 --> 00:22:58.818
Welcome to Bayonne, New Jersey.
Pimple on God's ass.

263
00:22:58.895 --> 00:23:01.557
Chief Sunday, we never met,
but I served with you on the Hoist.

264
00:23:03.266 --> 00:23:06.168
U.S.S. Hoist.
I 'spect I 'member you now.

265
00:23:07.237 --> 00:23:09.171
So what's for chow, cookie?

266
00:23:09.239 --> 00:23:12.208
I wouldn't know, Chief.
I'm reporting for diving school.

267
00:23:12.276 --> 00:23:14.767
Oh, yeah, that's right.

268
00:23:14.845 --> 00:23:17.871
They say you wrote over 100 letters
requesting admission to this school.

269
00:23:17.948 --> 00:23:19.882
You got you
some grit in you, huh?

270
00:23:19.950 --> 00:23:24.718
- Yes, sir.
- Well, it's gonna be a hot one today.

271
00:23:30.628 --> 00:23:33.927
Sure hope you're better
than the last cook.
That man's food could kill your dog.

272
00:23:36.334 --> 00:23:38.894
Chief.

273
00:23:54.186 --> 00:23:56.120
- Thank you.
- All righteous.

274
00:23:56.188 --> 00:23:58.123
There you go.

275
00:24:21.048 --> 00:24:23.778
Had yourself
anything to drink today?

276
00:24:23.851 --> 00:24:26.149
No, sir, Chief.

277
00:24:26.220 --> 00:24:28.882
What say we go on into town
and get us a nice cold one?

278
00:24:28.956 --> 00:24:31.754
I can't do that, Chief.
I haven't reported for duty.

279
00:24:31.826 --> 00:24:35.763
I tell you what.
I'll buy you a tall one over there.

280
00:24:35.831 --> 00:24:40.325
A bus ticket too, so you can go back
to whatever burg you sprang from.

281
00:24:40.402 --> 00:24:43.132
What do you say?

282
00:24:43.205 --> 00:24:45.366
Sir, I am a Navy man.

283
00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:47.704
Where I come from,
there are no oceans.

284
00:24:47.776 --> 00:24:50.904
Only dirt farms
and ornery mules.

285
00:24:52.715 --> 00:24:57.277
And no self-respecting Navy man
makes a living driving mules.

286
00:25:02.825 --> 00:25:05.453
Sir.

287
00:25:13.937 --> 00:25:15.871
You know what the Chinese say,
cookie?

288
00:25:18.809 --> 00:25:21.334
Beware what you wish for.

289
00:25:24.114 --> 00:25:27.015
I stole a pie! I stole a pie!
- Let him in.

290
00:25:28.920 --> 00:25:32.014
I stole a pie! I stole a pie!

291
00:25:32.090 --> 00:25:35.787
I stole a pie!
I stole a pie!

292
00:25:35.860 --> 00:25:39.193
I stole a pie!
I stole a pie!

293
00:25:42.300 --> 00:25:46.361
Get in there.
Go on. Hoist away.

294
00:26:02.755 --> 00:26:05.452
Do-Do-Do-Don't stare at him.

295
00:26:05.525 --> 00:26:08.050
- Who is he?
- The commanding officer,

296
00:26:08.128 --> 00:26:11.894
b-b-but everyone calls him
M-M-Mr. Pappy.

297
00:26:11.965 --> 00:26:13.865
- He's a war hero.
- Here.

298
00:26:13.934 --> 00:26:16.300
They, they were gonna make him
an admiral up in D. C....

299
00:26:16.369 --> 00:26:20.738
'f-f-fore they,
they found out he's got more,
more screws loose than a Studebaker.

300
00:26:20.807 --> 00:26:26.337
So they sent him here.
Better salute him or you'll be
spending your first night in the brig.

301
00:26:28.749 --> 00:26:30.683
I stole a pie!

302
00:26:33.354 --> 00:26:36.255
Come on. I'll show you the barracks.

303
00:27:01.718 --> 00:27:03.379
Attention on deck!

304
00:27:12.028 --> 00:27:15.122
Gentlemen, in 1948,

305
00:27:15.198 --> 00:27:18.498
President Harry S. Truman
had the courage and forward-thinking
and enlightenment...

306
00:27:18.569 --> 00:27:21.163
to desegregate
the United States military.

307
00:27:21.238 --> 00:27:26.403
Now I want y'all to welcome the Bayonne
Diving School's first colored trainee,

308
00:27:26.477 --> 00:27:29.275
Bosun's Mate
Second Class Carl Brashear.

309
00:27:34.051 --> 00:27:37.317
I don't hear anyone welcomin'
Bosun's Mate Brashear.

310
00:27:42.727 --> 00:27:46.561
Master Chief,
no disrespect to the president,

311
00:27:47.632 --> 00:27:49.623
but I don't bunk with niggers.

312
00:29:03.345 --> 00:29:07.214
- Aren't you gonna go too?
- N-N-N-No.

313
00:29:08.485 --> 00:29:10.851
I-I-I-I'm from Wisconsin.

314
00:29:12.622 --> 00:29:14.556
Never been there.

315
00:29:20.930 --> 00:29:23.398
Haily gets a fast ball
low and inside for strike three,

316
00:29:23.466 --> 00:29:25.867
and Jackie Robinson strikes out.

317
00:29:32.176 --> 00:29:36.374
And the score as we had it
Brooklyn, one, Milwaukee, one.

318
00:29:44.289 --> 00:29:47.053
Rise and shine, cookie.
Time for trainin'.

319
00:29:52.531 --> 00:29:55.830
- Are you familiar with
the principle of Boyle's Law?

320
00:29:55.901 --> 00:29:57.630
The what?

321
00:29:57.703 --> 00:30:00.400
I didn't hear your answer.

322
00:30:03.786 --> 00:30:06.016
Come on, cookie.
Get up.

323
00:30:06.088 --> 00:30:09.251
- Boyle's Law states that,
at a constant temperature,

324
00:30:09.325 --> 00:30:14.262
the volume of a confined ideal gas
varies inversely with its pressure!

325
00:30:14.330 --> 00:30:17.925
- Now why is this law
important in divin'?
- I don't know, Chief!

326
00:30:18.000 --> 00:30:21.266
You ain't never gonna know,
'cause you're just some dumb
dirt nigger from Podunk!

327
00:30:21.338 --> 00:30:25.604
I know you.
Your sweet smell hung in every bunk
and goddamn shack I ever lived in.

328
00:30:25.676 --> 00:30:29.237
Your nigger face stared at me
every time we had to leave...

329
00:30:29.313 --> 00:30:31.645
'cause your daddy
could farm it cheaper than mine.

330
00:30:31.715 --> 00:30:35.207
Mine drank himself into a $7 casket,
but that ain't gonna happen to me...

331
00:30:35.285 --> 00:30:37.481
because I'm a Master Diver!

332
00:30:37.555 --> 00:30:41.958
Maybe you'll remember that next time
you imply we got anything in common!

333
00:30:42.026 --> 00:30:43.994
You read me, cookie?

334
00:30:46.464 --> 00:30:48.796
- What?
- Get your goddamn Wisconsin ass...

335
00:30:48.867 --> 00:30:51.597
back to bed, Snowhill!

336
00:31:21.535 --> 00:31:25.665
The men you are watching
are going to be Navy divers.

337
00:31:25.739 --> 00:31:29.106
You bottom suckers are not fit
to observe them.

338
00:31:29.175 --> 00:31:31.303
Avert your eyes!

339
00:31:31.379 --> 00:31:34.212
My name is Master Chief
Billy Sunday.

340
00:31:34.282 --> 00:31:37.547
There's a preacher by the same
name cleaned up Chicago...

341
00:31:37.618 --> 00:31:41.349
of all the whorin' spics, drunken wops
and motherfuckin' niggers...

342
00:31:41.422 --> 00:31:45.722
that was makin' that place unfit
for decent white folks to live.

343
00:31:45.793 --> 00:31:48.957
The only difference between me
and that old preacher...

344
00:31:49.031 --> 00:31:52.523
is that he worked for God
and I am God!

345
00:31:55.637 --> 00:31:59.801
Now, why don't the first ten of
you Girl Scouts step forward?

346
00:31:59.875 --> 00:32:02.343
Come on!
Drop your dicks! Let's go!

347
00:32:04.446 --> 00:32:06.641
Three quarters of you
standing here today...

348
00:32:06.715 --> 00:32:09.276
will fail
to become Navy divers.

349
00:32:09.352 --> 00:32:12.321
Three from the first row,
step forward. Step forward!

350
00:32:16.259 --> 00:32:18.420
Of those unfortunates
that do pass,

351
00:32:18.494 --> 00:32:21.054
only three of you will live
to reach retirement...

352
00:32:21.130 --> 00:32:24.224
'cause divin'is the most
dangerous job in the Navy.

353
00:32:25.803 --> 00:32:28.237
So who wants to quit?

354
00:32:28.305 --> 00:32:30.330
Say it now,
who wants to quit?

355
00:32:30.407 --> 00:32:33.740
You got somethin' to offer,
huh?

356
00:32:36.880 --> 00:32:42.079
Who wants to save me the sweat
of training your sorry ass?

357
00:32:42.152 --> 00:32:44.883
You? You?

358
00:32:44.956 --> 00:32:46.890
Cookie?

359
00:32:51.029 --> 00:32:53.964
You?

360
00:32:54.032 --> 00:32:56.899
You gonna look me
in the eye, son, huh?

361
00:32:58.103 --> 00:33:00.799
What are you,
some kind of broke-dick Popeye?

362
00:33:02.475 --> 00:33:05.638
Huh? Let me guess.

363
00:33:05.711 --> 00:33:07.770
You were captain
of the swim team, weren't you?

364
00:33:07.847 --> 00:33:11.783
You and your girlfriend used
to practice the breast stroke!

365
00:33:16.489 --> 00:33:18.480
Say it
like you got a pair!

366
00:33:18.557 --> 00:33:21.391
- My w-w-w-wife.
- Oh, that's right.

367
00:33:21.461 --> 00:33:24.953
It's in your record.
You knocked her up sophomore year.

368
00:33:25.032 --> 00:33:28.524
Well, maybe you can bring
the little w-w-w-woman down one night...

369
00:33:28.602 --> 00:33:32.197
and all the boys can practice
the b-b-b-breast stroke.

370
00:33:34.675 --> 00:33:38.908
I heard you were a hell of a swimmer,
Snowhill. State champ?

371
00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:41.847
Y-Yes, y-yes,
M-Master Chief.

372
00:33:45.687 --> 00:33:48.315
Snowhill,
please step forward.

373
00:33:48.389 --> 00:33:50.323
Come on.

374
00:33:51.392 --> 00:33:53.326
About face.

375
00:33:57.199 --> 00:33:59.861
You let go before I relieve you,

376
00:33:59.935 --> 00:34:03.166
you fail my course right now,
got it, swim champ?

377
00:34:10.446 --> 00:34:14.816
Swimmin' don't got dick shit
to do with deep-sea divin'.

378
00:34:14.884 --> 00:34:16.909
If Johnny fuckin' Weismuller
were in the soup...

379
00:34:16.986 --> 00:34:19.546
wearin' a 200-pound
Mark Five divin' rig,

380
00:34:19.622 --> 00:34:21.556
he couldn't swim
to fuck Esther Williams...

381
00:34:21.624 --> 00:34:24.320
if she was three feet
in front of him buck naked.

382
00:34:24.394 --> 00:34:26.988
The only way to survive
is to trust each other,

383
00:34:27.063 --> 00:34:29.190
'cause underwater all you got
is the man next to you.

384
00:34:29.265 --> 00:34:32.360
And that is why the only men
that get through my course...

385
00:34:32.436 --> 00:34:34.495
are the very, very best.

386
00:34:34.572 --> 00:34:36.506
Now get out of my sight.

387
00:34:38.075 --> 00:34:40.305
Boy, I don't know.

388
00:34:47.785 --> 00:34:49.844
Permission to relieve
the man below, Master Chief.

389
00:34:49.920 --> 00:34:53.254
What are you, cookie,
some kind of goddamn hero?

390
00:34:53.325 --> 00:34:56.192
I got no room in my class for heroes
or stutterin' swim champs...

391
00:34:56.261 --> 00:34:58.855
with a wife and kids
to worry about, do you read me?

392
00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:02.491
If you wanna flunk me, flunk me, but
don't punish him for being decent to me.

393
00:35:02.567 --> 00:35:06.435
I don't have to flunk you.
You're gonna do that all on your own.
He had half a chance.

394
00:35:06.505 --> 00:35:09.168
He still does.
Permission to relieve him.

395
00:35:09.242 --> 00:35:12.871
Claims he can hold his breath over four
minutes. Hell, it ain't even been two.

396
00:35:12.945 --> 00:35:16.847
- I believe Gunner's Mate
Snowhill's a liar!

397
00:35:16.916 --> 00:35:20.079
Now we're men of honor, ain't we,
cookie? We don't abide liars.

398
00:35:20.153 --> 00:35:22.747
You're out of my program,
Snowhill.

399
00:35:22.822 --> 00:35:25.450
Bosun's Mate Brashear,
you have the barracks to yourself.

400
00:35:28.362 --> 00:35:30.762
Damn!

401
00:35:30.831 --> 00:35:32.765
The Navy diver
is not a fighting man.

402
00:35:32.833 --> 00:35:36.098
He is a salvage expert.
If it's lost underwater, he finds it.

403
00:35:36.170 --> 00:35:39.401
If it's sunk, he brings it up.
If it's in the way, he moves it.

404
00:35:39.473 --> 00:35:42.772
If he's lucky, he'll die young
200 feet beneath the waves...

405
00:35:42.843 --> 00:35:45.108
for that is the closest he will
ever get to being a hero.

406
00:35:45.180 --> 00:35:48.581
Hell, I don't know why anybody'd
want to be a Navy diver.

407
00:35:48.650 --> 00:35:52.051
Good flange work, Rourke.
Almost there.

408
00:35:52.120 --> 00:35:54.054
Thank you, Master Chief.

409
00:36:01.930 --> 00:36:04.033
Machinist's Mate Rourke, 91.

410
00:36:04.033 --> 00:36:04.328
Machinist's Mate Rourke, 91.

411
00:36:04.400 --> 00:36:08.632
Bosun's Mate Brashear, 37.

412
00:36:08.704 --> 00:36:12.367
- If you fail the next test,
you're out of the program.
- Yes, sir.

413
00:36:12.441 --> 00:36:16.673
There are seats of learning beyond
the walls and control of this camp.

414
00:36:22.886 --> 00:36:26.344
Ladies,
this is weekend liberty.

415
00:36:26.423 --> 00:36:31.759
Anyone's ass
that ain't back here on time
will have to answer to me personally.

416
00:36:31.828 --> 00:36:35.389
And remember, ladies, one-night stands
may be over by mornin',

417
00:36:35.465 --> 00:36:38.161
but syp hilis lasts
a lifetime.

418
00:36:38.235 --> 00:36:41.569
Dismissed!

419
00:36:47.044 --> 00:36:51.481
Watch out.

420
00:36:56.220 --> 00:36:58.155
- Have fun, baby.
- Flowers!

421
00:36:58.223 --> 00:37:01.818
Flowers! Hey, how about some flowers
for your young lady, huh?

422
00:37:18.044 --> 00:37:20.137
What's the hitch?

423
00:37:24.150 --> 00:37:27.142
- You're the one who called.
- Yes, ma'am.

424
00:37:27.220 --> 00:37:31.122
I told you. We're a public library,

425
00:37:31.190 --> 00:37:33.887
not a tutoring service.

426
00:37:33.961 --> 00:37:38.591
Now, if you don't mind,
there is a Mr. Biddle at home.

427
00:37:38.666 --> 00:37:41.157
In fact, he's probably
brought flowers.

428
00:37:55.450 --> 00:37:58.977
Have a wonderful weekend.
And lock up, would you?

429
00:37:59.054 --> 00:38:02.888
- Uh-huh.
- And be sure to kick him out.

430
00:38:04.025 --> 00:38:08.294
- Hello.
- We're closed.

431
00:38:08.427 --> 00:38:13.058
Not for three minutes.
You studying on nursin'?

432
00:38:13.133 --> 00:38:16.261
A person doesn't "study on"
anything, Bosun's Mate.

433
00:38:19.172 --> 00:38:22.835
You know your rates and ranks. Did you
get that from one of these books?

434
00:38:25.445 --> 00:38:28.381
Look, I'm not here
to flirt with you.

435
00:38:28.449 --> 00:38:31.247
I'm in diving school
across the river.

436
00:38:31.319 --> 00:38:35.085
I'm not just good at it.
I was born for it.

437
00:38:35.156 --> 00:38:38.216
But the joke is, I'm gonna wash out
if I don't pass my next exam.

438
00:38:38.292 --> 00:38:40.726
What was the last grade
you completed in school?

439
00:38:40.795 --> 00:38:43.787
- Seventh.
- I can't help you.

440
00:38:43.865 --> 00:38:47.063
- Why not?
- Because it took me four years
of working at places like this...

441
00:38:47.136 --> 00:38:49.070
to get through med school.

442
00:38:49.138 --> 00:38:52.630
Now I have six weeks to study for
my exam. I pass, I become an intern,

443
00:38:52.708 --> 00:38:54.869
and maybe someday
become a doctor.

444
00:38:54.943 --> 00:38:58.902
You're too far behind,
and I don't have the time.

445
00:38:58.981 --> 00:39:02.109
Okay. Go on.
Walk around reading to yourself.

446
00:39:02.184 --> 00:39:04.813
- Don't give me another thought.
Just go on.
- Don't you get it?

447
00:39:04.888 --> 00:39:08.221
Whether I help you or not doesn't
matter. You're gonna fail anyway.

448
00:39:08.291 --> 00:39:12.785
I won't. I can't.

449
00:39:15.231 --> 00:39:17.290
Why do you want this
so badly?

450
00:39:17.367 --> 00:39:19.665
Because they said
I couldn't have it.

451
00:39:39.958 --> 00:39:42.791
I may know
a professor at City--

452
00:40:29.042 --> 00:40:34.743
Boyle's Law describes
the behavior of gases undervarying
amounts of atmospheric pressure.

453
00:40:34.816 --> 00:40:38.650
It states that if a diver
holds his breath at 100 feet,

454
00:40:38.720 --> 00:40:40.984
continues holding while rising
to ten feet,

455
00:40:41.055 --> 00:40:44.354
then the gases in his lungs
increase four times.

456
00:40:44.425 --> 00:40:46.359
Now why is this important
to a diver?

457
00:40:46.427 --> 00:40:48.759
Forget to exhale on the way up,
and your lungs explode.

458
00:40:52.300 --> 00:40:56.294
I can work with you,
but my time is precious.

459
00:40:56.372 --> 00:41:00.001
So the first time you go out
drinking and fighting...

460
00:41:00.075 --> 00:41:03.044
and leave me waiting here,
our arrangement ends.

461
00:41:08.017 --> 00:41:10.417
Good morning.

462
00:41:19.963 --> 00:41:25.230
I, um... have to open up.

463
00:41:25.302 --> 00:41:27.964
Now are you gonna tell me your
name, or is it still a secret?

464
00:41:28.038 --> 00:41:30.974
My name is Jo.

465
00:41:32.443 --> 00:41:35.071
My father always wanted
a boy.

466
00:41:36.213 --> 00:41:38.773
He was in the Navy too.

467
00:41:38.849 --> 00:41:43.218
- Is he still active?
- I haven't seen him since I was nine.

468
00:41:57.469 --> 00:41:59.903
Mm-mm, mm-mm.
Like this.

469
00:42:06.946 --> 00:42:09.073
- Good night.
- Good night.

470
00:42:10.750 --> 00:42:13.241
Fire Controlman Mellegrano, 91.

471
00:42:13.319 --> 00:42:17.119
Mate DuBoyce, 85.
Engineman Crofoot, 69.

472
00:42:17.190 --> 00:42:21.286
Bosun's Mate
Carl Brashear,

473
00:42:21.361 --> 00:42:23.296
76.

474
00:42:32.906 --> 00:42:35.136
Boots, cookie,
tear yourselves away, ladies.

475
00:42:35.209 --> 00:42:38.406
You're next in the water. You're gonna
go down to the training vessel,

476
00:42:38.479 --> 00:42:42.541
patch ahole so we canpump her full
of air and raise her to the surface.

477
00:42:42.617 --> 00:42:45.950
Then we're gonna sink her
and do it again.

478
00:42:46.020 --> 00:42:50.855
Because underwater,
all you've got is the man next to you!

479
00:42:50.925 --> 00:42:53.291
Chief, what the hell's
goin' on down there?

480
00:42:53.361 --> 00:42:55.886
That boy stays down there any longer,
he's gonna start gettin' mail.

481
00:43:04.907 --> 00:43:07.671
Isert, come on.
Finish torching that hole.

482
00:43:07.743 --> 00:43:09.711
I'm tryin',
but this thing's real awkward.

483
00:43:11.347 --> 00:43:13.747
- How's it look?
- Looks like hell.

484
00:43:13.816 --> 00:43:16.250
Green Diver, this is
Master Chief Sunday.

485
00:43:16.318 --> 00:43:20.653
You have three minutes
to get your patch hot and hung
before the next team comes down.

486
00:43:20.724 --> 00:43:22.851
Nowcome on, Isert!
Move your raggedy ass!

487
00:43:22.926 --> 00:43:24.894
- RedDiver?
- Yes, Master Chief.

488
00:43:24.961 --> 00:43:28.089
God damn it, Rourke, I've had girlfriends
that could weld faster than that.

489
00:43:28.165 --> 00:43:30.725
Now move him along.

490
00:43:30.801 --> 00:43:34.362
- Come on, Isert. Now hang your patch.
- Yeah, okay, Rourke. I'm trying.

491
00:43:41.479 --> 00:43:44.846
- Hey, Isert, you feel that?
- Do I feel what?

492
00:43:46.150 --> 00:43:48.618
What the hell?

493
00:43:48.686 --> 00:43:52.588
Topside, this wreck is moving!

494
00:43:52.657 --> 00:43:54.853
She's limping, Chief!
We're sliding down!

495
00:43:54.927 --> 00:43:57.691
Somebody tell me
what just happened?

496
00:43:57.763 --> 00:44:00.027
- Top side!
- Get it! Grab that hose!

497
00:44:14.814 --> 00:44:18.750
- Red Diver, what's your situation?
- The ship just dropped 50 feet.

498
00:44:18.818 --> 00:44:22.310
- We landed on something.
- Better bring those boys home
till we figure this out.

499
00:44:22.388 --> 00:44:26.552
- Square yourselves away.
You're coming home.
- Negative on the come home.

500
00:44:26.626 --> 00:44:28.992
Isert's got his air hose tangled.

501
00:44:29.062 --> 00:44:32.692
- My air hose is stuck!
- Fouled. Now get it unfouled.

502
00:44:36.570 --> 00:44:38.936
Rourke, what's wrong?
Why are we movin'?

503
00:44:39.006 --> 00:44:41.474
- We slipped partway
down the channel bank.
- Rourke!

504
00:44:45.312 --> 00:44:49.249
- This wreck is live!
- You get this off!

505
00:44:49.317 --> 00:44:51.808
- I'm gonna have to change out
his lifeline and air hose.
- Listen, Rourke.

506
00:44:51.887 --> 00:44:55.118
He's your buddy.
You follow his line back,
unfoul it and get him out of there.

507
00:44:55.190 --> 00:44:57.681
I'm trying, but it's just too tight.
Send down a line!

508
00:44:59.561 --> 00:45:01.654
Help!

509
00:45:01.730 --> 00:45:03.857
- I need help down here.
- Help's on the way.

510
00:45:03.932 --> 00:45:06.333
- I'm ready, Master Chief.
- Dennis, undress him.

511
00:45:06.402 --> 00:45:10.930
- You can't go down there.
- Better not be talking to me.
I won't haveyour familiar tone.

512
00:45:12.174 --> 00:45:15.666
You can't dive that deep.
I'm ready. Let me go.

513
00:45:23.710 --> 00:45:26.578
Master Chief, it looks
like the ship slid down...

514
00:45:26.647 --> 00:45:29.878
on some discharge pipes
coming from that factory.

515
00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:34.046
They give out, and this whole ship's
going right to the bottom.

516
00:45:34.121 --> 00:45:37.784
You don't worry about
that boat.Just get that hose to Rourke.

517
00:45:44.432 --> 00:45:46.832
For God's sake!

518
00:45:46.902 --> 00:45:50.360
What the hell was that, cookie?
- Look!

519
00:45:50.438 --> 00:45:52.633
The ship's weight is crushing
those pipes, Chief.

520
00:45:52.707 --> 00:45:55.505
Gotta get him on a fresh hose
and out of here fast!

521
00:45:55.577 --> 00:46:00.014
Topside, Blue Diver's here.
He's gota fresh line.

522
00:46:00.081 --> 00:46:03.347
All right, lsert.
Rourke's gonna change you out, and
you're gonna be walking out of there.

523
00:46:03.419 --> 00:46:07.082
- Okay.
- That boy's got five minutes
of air if he don't panic.

524
00:46:07.156 --> 00:46:09.522
You screw up the change out,
and that boy's dead, read me?

525
00:46:09.592 --> 00:46:12.993
- Yes, Master Chief.
- Isert, we're not gonna be able
to talk for a few minutes.

526
00:46:13.062 --> 00:46:15.826
I want you to think of your favorite
song, and I want you tosing it.

527
00:46:15.898 --> 00:46:19.733
- I don't know any songs.
- You got to slow your respiration.
Breathe easy.

528
00:46:19.803 --> 00:46:23.603
- Just breathe easy.
- Please. I wasn't made for this.

529
00:46:23.674 --> 00:46:27.371
I want to go home now!
I want to go home now!

530
00:46:27.444 --> 00:46:29.378
Would you let me
come home now?

531
00:46:29.446 --> 00:46:33.746
I want to quit!l want to quit!
I really want to quit!

532
00:46:33.817 --> 00:46:36.753
- I want to quit!
- Change him out now!

533
00:46:39.958 --> 00:46:43.121
- She's movin', Chief!
- Come on, Rourke! I got him!

534
00:46:48.199 --> 00:46:51.726
Topside, Isert's off air.

535
00:46:55.207 --> 00:46:57.698
- What's going on down there?
- She's gonna roll over!

536
00:46:57.776 --> 00:47:01.303
I 'spect so. You stay down there,
and you change that boy out, hear me?

537
00:47:03.015 --> 00:47:06.416
- Rourke!
- I'm out of here!

538
00:47:06.485 --> 00:47:08.419
I gotta get out of here!
She's going down!

539
00:47:08.487 --> 00:47:10.580
- Rourke, come back here!
- Rourke!

540
00:47:10.656 --> 00:47:13.251
- Rourke, get back here!
- I ain't dying!

541
00:47:13.326 --> 00:47:15.260
- Rourke!
- I'm out of here.

542
00:47:15.328 --> 00:47:18.297
Don't leave!
Carl, don't leave me!

543
00:47:18.365 --> 00:47:22.358
I need my air hose!
I can't breathe, Carl!

544
00:47:22.435 --> 00:47:24.369
I'm getting dizzy!

545
00:47:50.766 --> 00:47:53.166
I can't breathe.

546
00:48:07.583 --> 00:48:11.212
- Topside, he's blacking out!
- Goddamn it, hook him up!

547
00:48:13.289 --> 00:48:16.725
I got it!

548
00:48:36.080 --> 00:48:39.811
- We're coming home, Chief.
- Never doubted it.

549
00:49:09.748 --> 00:49:12.876
Machinist Mate First Class Rourke,
front and center!

550
00:49:25.398 --> 00:49:28.196
"The president of the
United States of America...

551
00:49:28.268 --> 00:49:31.863
takes great pleasure inpresenting
the Navy and Marine Corps
Medal of Heroism...

552
00:49:31.938 --> 00:49:35.032
to Machinist Mate First Class
Dylan Rourke,

553
00:49:35.108 --> 00:49:38.772
whereby Petty Officer Rourke
on the 22nd of September...

554
00:49:38.846 --> 00:49:41.076
of the year 1952,

555
00:49:41.149 --> 00:49:43.083
with apparent disregard
for his own life,

556
00:49:43.151 --> 00:49:47.485
did, at Bayonne, New Jersey,
save the life of
Petty Officer Timothy Douglas Isert."

557
00:50:09.244 --> 00:50:11.178
Post.

558
00:50:21.925 --> 00:50:24.155
Class 0252 dismissed.

559
00:50:58.797 --> 00:51:02.255
- Carl?
- Hey, I got your telegram.

560
00:51:02.334 --> 00:51:05.462
No, no, no. I got the wire.
How's Daddy doing?

561
00:51:05.537 --> 00:51:07.971
Is he up and around again?

562
00:51:21.320 --> 00:51:24.016
Yeah! Yeah!

563
00:52:22.686 --> 00:52:26.053
Hello? Carl? Is that you?

564
00:52:26.122 --> 00:52:29.182
Hey,Jo.
Hey, it's me.

565
00:52:29.259 --> 00:52:31.420
Where are you?
Are you okay?

566
00:52:31.494 --> 00:52:34.725
No, I'm okay. I'm okay.

567
00:52:34.798 --> 00:52:39.759
Uh, listen, uh,

568
00:52:39.837 --> 00:52:41.771
c-could you meet me?

569
00:52:43.941 --> 00:52:47.069
- Goddamn it!
- Okay. I'll stay here.

570
00:52:47.144 --> 00:52:52.810
Damn it! The miserable son of a bitch
in there drinkin' on my anniversary!

571
00:53:03.228 --> 00:53:05.958
You're the one, aren'tyou?

572
00:53:09.701 --> 00:53:11.931
Well, I'm Gwen... Sunday.

573
00:53:21.814 --> 00:53:23.839
Sorry to hear that.

574
00:53:32.658 --> 00:53:35.628
You know he's gonna
kick you out of the Navy.

575
00:53:40.701 --> 00:53:43.192
He's gonna kick you out
of diving.

576
00:53:49.576 --> 00:53:52.842
So what
you gonna do about it?

577
00:53:52.914 --> 00:53:56.145
You just gonna let him run you over,
just like you do everyone else?

578
00:54:01.790 --> 00:54:04.486
You know, he's in there
right now.

579
00:54:06.661 --> 00:54:09.186
He wanted a party,

580
00:54:09.264 --> 00:54:11.597
let's give him one.

581
00:54:16.595 --> 00:54:18.392
- She told me...

582
00:54:18.464 --> 00:54:21.194
it was okay
to dance with a girl.

583
00:54:28.775 --> 00:54:31.369
Oh, llove this song!

584
00:54:40.754 --> 00:54:44.884
Donny, be a dear lad
and get us two scotches.

585
00:54:44.958 --> 00:54:49.623
- We're out.
- Lucky for us, you got
a whole bar full of bourbon.

586
00:55:01.309 --> 00:55:03.334
What the hell are you doing,
bringin' him in here?

587
00:55:08.150 --> 00:55:12.246
- Get out.
- Well, I'll be goddamned.

588
00:55:12.321 --> 00:55:15.188
It's prom night
here at the Moor Bar.

589
00:55:15.257 --> 00:55:18.693
You boys, you have
a drink on me. Go ahead.

590
00:55:23.166 --> 00:55:25.396
Hell, I don't know
who classes up the joint more--

591
00:55:25.468 --> 00:55:29.234
the fetching young lady
in the fur stole or cookie here.

592
00:55:29.305 --> 00:55:34.333
So what'd you two kids come here
to do anyway? Dance?

593
00:55:34.410 --> 00:55:38.210
Why not take a turn?
It's a free country, mostly.

594
00:55:38.281 --> 00:55:40.750
You made a big mistake,
walking in here, cookie.

595
00:55:40.818 --> 00:55:45.084
- Oh, it's my fault.
- It's all your fault.

596
00:55:45.155 --> 00:55:49.114
Spoiled little rich girl gets her kicks
draggin' stray men in here.

597
00:55:49.193 --> 00:55:54.130
Thinks we're just
a bunch of sweaty rednecks
she can shake up for the fun of it.

598
00:55:54.198 --> 00:55:59.159
Hey, Donny, bea dearlad
and bring the lady a fresh soldier.

599
00:56:00.605 --> 00:56:02.766
Think you deserve a beer,
don't you?

600
00:56:02.841 --> 00:56:05.503
Fraternizing among Navy men.

601
00:56:05.577 --> 00:56:08.102
Think you're
as good as they are?

602
00:56:08.179 --> 00:56:10.113
How 'bout me, cookie?
You better than me?

603
00:56:10.181 --> 00:56:12.911
- You're damn right, I am.
- Mm-hmm.

604
00:56:18.724 --> 00:56:20.749
You see this pipe?

605
00:56:20.826 --> 00:56:25.525
General MacArthur himself
smoked this pipe.

606
00:56:25.598 --> 00:56:27.657
I served with him
in Leyte Gulf.

607
00:56:27.733 --> 00:56:29.928
Biggest naval battle
in history.

608
00:56:30.002 --> 00:56:33.369
Kamikaze ripped into this escort
carrier, name of Saint Lo.

609
00:56:33.439 --> 00:56:38.969
She went down on a shallow reef,
trapping me and six boys
in the fire room.

610
00:56:39.045 --> 00:56:41.843
- Only one way out.
- Flood the compartment and swim up.

611
00:56:41.915 --> 00:56:46.045
Five decks, cookie.
Five fuckin' decks.

612
00:56:46.119 --> 00:56:48.349
Locked bulk heads,
dead bodies everywhere.

613
00:56:48.422 --> 00:56:52.951
You got to have your balls
screwed on tight for that swim.

614
00:56:53.027 --> 00:56:57.020
We still had intercom. Old MacArthur
himself came over that squawk box,

615
00:56:57.098 --> 00:56:59.032
"Sunday,
you cocky son of a bitch,

616
00:56:59.100 --> 00:57:03.332
I bet you can't hold your breath for
four minutes and swim out of there."

617
00:57:03.404 --> 00:57:06.032
Know what I said back?

618
00:57:06.107 --> 00:57:10.305
" No, Mac, I can't, but
I'll bet you your cob pipe...

619
00:57:10.378 --> 00:57:13.712
I can hold it for five, 'cause that's
what it's gonna take, motherfucker."

620
00:57:13.782 --> 00:57:16.717
- C-C-C-Carl, this ain't worth--
- Get your hands off me.

621
00:57:16.785 --> 00:57:20.482
There's six men still breathin' today,
'cause I led 'em out of that fire room.

622
00:57:20.556 --> 00:57:24.014
And now just 'cause you pulled little
Isert's white little fuckin' ass...

623
00:57:24.092 --> 00:57:27.721
out of some row boat
sunk in a mud puddle,
you think you're better than me?

624
00:57:27.796 --> 00:57:30.027
Well, let's just see.

625
00:57:37.407 --> 00:57:40.899
What's your bet, cookie?

626
00:57:40.977 --> 00:57:44.743
- Put Snowhill back in diving.
- What do you owe him?

627
00:57:44.814 --> 00:57:47.215
- Nothing. You owe him.
- Oh, yeah?

628
00:57:47.284 --> 00:57:52.119
Fine. If I win, you ship out,
tonight. Deal?

629
00:57:55.759 --> 00:57:58.319
Deal.

630
00:57:58.395 --> 00:58:02.164
Show him, Master Chief!

631
00:58:02.998 --> 00:58:05.091
Will you be my tender?

632
00:58:05.167 --> 00:58:07.602
- Yeah.
- Let's go.

633
00:58:10.674 --> 00:58:13.871
Come on, baby!

634
00:58:33.964 --> 00:58:35.955
Let's go, baby!

635
00:58:37.802 --> 00:58:40.327
Come on, now.

636
00:58:44.743 --> 00:58:47.234
Come on, Sunday!

637
00:58:50.982 --> 00:58:55.146
- Go!
- Come on, Master ChiefSunday!

638
00:59:10.436 --> 00:59:13.462
One minute,
fifteen seconds.

639
00:59:39.033 --> 00:59:42.491
Two minutes, twenty-five seconds.

640
00:59:42.570 --> 00:59:46.028
Hey, it's another
ten bucks right here!

641
00:59:48.743 --> 00:59:50.711
Sunday, do it!

642
00:59:56.719 --> 01:00:00.314
Three minutes, ten seconds!

643
01:00:12.502 --> 01:00:15.232
Come on.

644
01:00:15.305 --> 01:00:18.172
- Four minutes!
- Four minutes! Four!

645
01:00:19.609 --> 01:00:21.543
- Stop it!
- No.

646
01:00:21.611 --> 01:00:24.409
- Chief.
- Stop it! Stop!

647
01:00:37.361 --> 01:00:41.957
Rourke, stop it!

648
01:00:46.971 --> 01:00:52.604
Carl, you-you okay?
Carl?

649
01:00:52.678 --> 01:00:55.977
- Carl?
- Chief Sunday, you all right?

650
01:00:56.048 --> 01:00:58.448
- Hold it!
- You all right, Chief Sunday?

651
01:00:58.517 --> 01:01:00.985
- I'm okay.
- Hold him up.

652
01:01:01.053 --> 01:01:03.487
- I got it.
- Hold it!

653
01:01:03.555 --> 01:01:06.319
- He's all right.
- Come on!

654
01:01:06.392 --> 01:01:08.326
Come on, hold him up!

655
01:01:08.394 --> 01:01:11.557
Let's go!

656
01:01:11.631 --> 01:01:15.123
She tried to drive off the pier
like a crazy woman!

657
01:01:15.201 --> 01:01:18.295
- Get her outta the car!
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!

658
01:01:18.371 --> 01:01:22.569
- Hey, hey.
- You know,
today's my wedding anniversary.

659
01:01:22.642 --> 01:01:24.941
You're gonna be all right.

660
01:01:25.012 --> 01:01:28.470
Come on, move, move.
Come on, babe.

661
01:01:28.549 --> 01:01:33.350
- No, not you, Billy!
- Come on, baby, come on.

662
01:01:33.420 --> 01:01:35.354
Bastard!

663
01:01:35.422 --> 01:01:38.585
Come on, baby. Come on.

664
01:01:41.161 --> 01:01:45.326
- Come on, baby, let's go home.
- Yeah?

665
01:01:45.400 --> 01:01:48.301
- Come on.
- Yeah?

666
01:01:48.370 --> 01:01:51.305
Go on home now. Nothin' to see here.

667
01:01:52.908 --> 01:01:54.842
Jo.

668
01:01:54.910 --> 01:01:56.844
Jo!

669
01:01:59.214 --> 01:02:03.379
I can't do this, Carl.
I can't live this life again.

670
01:02:03.452 --> 01:02:07.286
I pulled my father out of
more Navy bars than I care to count.

671
01:02:07.356 --> 01:02:10.814
-Jo, you don't know
what happened tonight.
- Oh, but I do.

672
01:02:15.164 --> 01:02:17.155
I passed my finals.

673
01:02:17.233 --> 01:02:20.567
Oh, I'm sorry.
I'm sorry,Jo.

674
01:02:20.637 --> 01:02:24.095
The point is, I'm gonna be
starting my internship at Bellevue.

675
01:02:24.174 --> 01:02:27.371
- It's gonna be crazy hours.
I won't have time to see you.
- I made a mistake.

676
01:02:27.444 --> 01:02:30.106
- It won't happen again.
- Oh, yes, it will.

677
01:02:30.180 --> 01:02:35.117
You wanted to fight that man.
You were just waiting for the moment.

678
01:02:35.185 --> 01:02:40.123
Don't you see...
I'm not like you?

679
01:02:40.191 --> 01:02:43.786
The things I want--

680
01:02:46.164 --> 01:02:50.430
The things I want
are smaller.

681
01:02:50.501 --> 01:02:53.231
If I just work hard
and keep my head down--

682
01:02:53.304 --> 01:02:56.570
Your whole life
will pass you by.

683
01:03:03.649 --> 01:03:07.085
Carl, most of what's
in those diving books...

684
01:03:07.152 --> 01:03:10.087
you know better than,
than me.

685
01:03:10.155 --> 01:03:13.819
You don't need me anymore.
You don't need anyone.

686
01:03:13.893 --> 01:03:16.384
I love you.

687
01:03:38.886 --> 01:03:40.820
Jo!

688
01:03:40.888 --> 01:03:43.049
Jo! Jo!

689
01:03:43.124 --> 01:03:46.719
- Jo! Hey,Jo!
- What?

690
01:03:46.794 --> 01:03:49.958
Jo! Marry me!

691
01:03:50.032 --> 01:03:52.500
He wants to know
if you'll marry him.

692
01:04:23.866 --> 01:04:25.101
Come in.

693
01:04:25.101 --> 01:04:26.034
Come in.

694
01:04:26.103 --> 01:04:29.266
Watch the door, Chief.
Try not to touch anything.

695
01:05:05.111 --> 01:05:08.478
Did you know
that ordinary house dust...

696
01:05:08.547 --> 01:05:11.710
is composed primarily
of human skin?

697
01:05:13.486 --> 01:05:15.545
No, sir,
I didn't know that.

698
01:05:15.621 --> 01:05:20.559
Makes you think twice
about who you invite into your home.

699
01:05:31.905 --> 01:05:34.396
Two table spoons
of machine oil...

700
01:05:34.474 --> 01:05:37.272
can contaminate...

701
01:05:37.344 --> 01:05:42.180
an entire ship's
fresh water supply.

702
01:05:44.352 --> 01:05:47.788
Some things just don't mix.

703
01:05:49.924 --> 01:05:52.757
Do they, Chief?

704
01:05:55.463 --> 01:05:58.024
He's gonna pass.

705
01:05:58.100 --> 01:06:01.627
Yesterday, he scored
a 94 onhis final.

706
01:06:01.703 --> 01:06:04.035
Sir, he don't have to be
that fast tomorrow.

707
01:06:04.106 --> 01:06:06.870
All he's got to do
is complete the exercise.

708
01:06:11.914 --> 01:06:14.611
Billy...

709
01:06:19.489 --> 01:06:23.289
there may come a day when a colored
diver graduates from this school,

710
01:06:23.359 --> 01:06:27.090
but it won't be tomorrow
or as long as I'm here.

711
01:06:29.165 --> 01:06:31.656
You agree with me,
of course.

712
01:06:33.204 --> 01:06:37.334
- Don't you, Chief?
- Yes, sir.

713
01:07:13.451 --> 01:07:16.045
Baseball season's
over, cookie.

714
01:07:17.789 --> 01:07:20.758
I figured Rourke.
I never even let myself think--

715
01:07:20.825 --> 01:07:24.283
- Why not?
- 'Cause I saw your last dive.

716
01:07:26.364 --> 01:07:30.301
You want to know what I am?
I'm the sorry son a bitch put here...

717
01:07:30.369 --> 01:07:34.465
to get through your thick fucking skull
that some things do not change.

718
01:07:34.540 --> 01:07:37.168
- I deserve to pass.
- Since when does deserving
mean anything?

719
01:07:37.243 --> 01:07:39.177
They ain't gonna have
a colored diver.

720
01:07:39.245 --> 01:07:42.806
'Cause no matter what you do, in their
eyes, you'll never be as good as them.

721
01:07:42.881 --> 01:07:45.180
- So, deserving or otherwise,
you're failing.
- No, you are.

722
01:07:45.252 --> 01:07:47.277
You think
I owe you somethin'?

723
01:07:47.354 --> 01:07:50.221
I don't owe you
a goddamn fucking thing.

724
01:07:50.290 --> 01:07:53.851
You or anybody else. You got fucked,
cookie. Happens to the best of us.

725
01:07:53.927 --> 01:07:56.760
You were right, Chief.
Youand I have nothing in common.

726
01:07:56.830 --> 01:08:00.732
I may be some dirt dumb nigger
from Podunk, but at least
I'm making something of myself.

727
01:08:00.800 --> 01:08:04.202
You, you're the same hateful,
little man you started out as.

728
01:08:04.272 --> 01:08:06.570
Without diving,
you're nothing...

729
01:08:06.641 --> 01:08:10.077
but a lost, broke-down son of a bitch
who used to be something.

730
01:08:26.828 --> 01:08:29.092
Hey!

731
01:08:29.164 --> 01:08:31.997
What did he say to you
to make you try so hard?

732
01:08:32.067 --> 01:08:34.399
" Be the best."

733
01:08:34.469 --> 01:08:36.562
Well, you are.

734
01:08:38.373 --> 01:08:42.310
Just don't show up tomorrow.
Pappy ain't gonna let you pass.

735
01:08:47.550 --> 01:08:49.882
What about you, Chief?

736
01:08:54.123 --> 01:08:57.855
Today will decide
which of you will become Navy Divers.

737
01:08:57.928 --> 01:09:02.388
The object of this test is to correctly
assemble this flange underwater.

738
01:09:02.466 --> 01:09:05.299
The pieces required for assembly
await you on the river bottom.

739
01:09:05.369 --> 01:09:09.738
Once you have located your project
flange, you will call for your tools.

740
01:09:09.807 --> 01:09:12.401
They will be lowered to you.

741
01:09:12.476 --> 01:09:16.937
You will be timed on your effort
and will accrue points
for a speedy completion.

742
01:09:17.015 --> 01:09:20.576
However, we'll keep pumping
air down to you for as long
as you can stand the cold.

743
01:09:20.652 --> 01:09:24.713
So take your time
and get it right.

744
01:09:51.517 --> 01:09:54.180
If you do not complete the flange,

745
01:09:54.254 --> 01:09:57.712
you have just wasted
six months of your lives.

746
01:10:08.635 --> 01:10:12.970
Divers, square yourselves away
and approach the rail.

747
01:10:54.017 --> 01:10:57.145
Topside, I have located
my work light.

748
01:11:17.741 --> 01:11:19.675
Topside, Blue Diver.

749
01:11:19.743 --> 01:11:22.941
I have located my project
and am requesting my toolbag.

750
01:11:23.014 --> 01:11:27.348
Topside, this is Red Diver.
I have located my project flange.

751
01:11:27.419 --> 01:11:31.515
- Requesting my tool bag.
- Tenders, lower your tool bags.

752
01:11:55.314 --> 01:11:58.374
Topside, Blue Diver.
I'm still waiting on my tool bag.

753
01:12:31.519 --> 01:12:34.818
Blue Diver, your tool bag
is on the river bottom.

754
01:12:51.440 --> 01:12:55.935
Chief, start the project time
on all divers.

755
01:13:20.738 --> 01:13:24.299
Machinist Mate Rourke,
one hour, thirty-seven minutes.

756
01:13:24.375 --> 01:13:27.139
Perfect assembly.

757
01:13:49.135 --> 01:13:53.196
Survey or Second Class Yarmouth,
two hours, nineteen minutes.

758
01:13:53.272 --> 01:13:55.900
Perfect assembly.

759
01:14:12.760 --> 01:14:15.024
I never thought
I'd live to see it.

760
01:14:15.095 --> 01:14:18.963
Four hours and nine minutes. Better
late than never, Engineman Crofoot.

761
01:14:19.033 --> 01:14:22.230
Perfect assembly.
How's the water down there?

762
01:14:22.302 --> 01:14:25.238
It's colder than
a well digger's ass, Master Chief.

763
01:14:25.306 --> 01:14:27.469
Take it inside.

764
01:15:05.942 --> 01:15:08.206
What do you mean,
he's still not up?

765
01:16:01.000 --> 01:16:03.798
Excuse me.

766
01:16:19.353 --> 01:16:21.344
Dive station,
Master Diver speaking.

767
01:16:21.422 --> 01:16:24.357
Chief Sunday, we have every cook
and shine boy in this camp...

768
01:16:24.425 --> 01:16:26.723
thinking they'll be next
to try a stunt like this.

769
01:16:26.794 --> 01:16:28.728
So you listen up.

770
01:16:28.796 --> 01:16:31.288
Don't bring him up
till he stops moving.

771
01:16:31.366 --> 01:16:33.300
He's near dead now, sir.

772
01:16:33.368 --> 01:16:35.563
Not till he stops moving,
Chief.

773
01:16:42.878 --> 01:16:44.846
Give it up, cookie.

774
01:16:44.913 --> 01:16:47.643
You go into shock down there,
you might not wake up.

775
01:16:47.716 --> 01:16:50.584
Come on, now.
This ain't worth dyin' for.

776
01:16:50.653 --> 01:16:52.848
M-My name is...

777
01:16:52.922 --> 01:16:56.688
Bosun's Mate Second Class...

778
01:16:56.759 --> 01:16:59.023
C-C-Carl Brashear.

779
01:17:01.230 --> 01:17:03.425
I am a Navy Diver.

780
01:17:28.760 --> 01:17:32.890
Bring him up.
Bring him up!

781
01:17:32.964 --> 01:17:34.898
- I got him.
- We're bringing him home.

782
01:17:34.966 --> 01:17:38.424
Sailor,
disregard that order!

783
01:17:40.004 --> 01:17:42.837
Sailor! Sailor!

784
01:17:42.907 --> 01:17:47.811
Chief Sunday,
effective immediately,

785
01:17:47.880 --> 01:17:51.281
I am relieving you
of your duties!

786
01:17:51.350 --> 01:17:53.784
Do you hear me, Chief?

787
01:17:56.689 --> 01:17:59.089
Hold the line.
Hold that line.

788
01:18:22.016 --> 01:18:25.645
Come on, Brashear.
You're almost there.

789
01:18:25.720 --> 01:18:29.053
Just a few more steps.
Come on, we'll help you.

790
01:18:31.859 --> 01:18:34.521
A little more.

791
01:18:34.595 --> 01:18:36.529
That's it.

792
01:18:45.407 --> 01:18:47.568
Open it up.

793
01:19:06.095 --> 01:19:08.359
Bosun's Mate Second Class
Carl Brashear,

794
01:19:08.431 --> 01:19:10.865
nine hours,
thirty-one minutes.

795
01:19:10.934 --> 01:19:13.563
Perfect assembly.

796
01:19:20.778 --> 01:19:22.712
Get him inside.

797
01:19:25.883 --> 01:19:28.511
Help him out!

798
01:19:40.398 --> 01:19:43.196
Carl, d-d-did y-y-you h-hear--

799
01:19:43.268 --> 01:19:45.998
-Slow down, Snowhill.
-They put me back in the diving program.

800
01:19:46.071 --> 01:19:48.596
- I start training next week.
- Congratulations.

801
01:19:48.673 --> 01:19:51.541
Thanks, Carl.

802
01:19:51.611 --> 01:19:54.842
Hey, I almost forgot.
Y-Y-You hear about Sunday?

803
01:19:54.914 --> 01:19:59.715
- No.
- M-Mr. Pappy blew a gasket
when the son of a bitch passed you.

804
01:19:59.785 --> 01:20:03.016
He b-busted him down ashred
and shipped him out.

805
01:20:03.089 --> 01:20:05.523
I guess that fucker
got his in the end, huh?

806
01:20:07.193 --> 01:20:09.594
I guess he did.

807
01:20:15.068 --> 01:20:17.093
Guess he did.

808
01:20:59.581 --> 01:21:03.951
Will you still say

809
01:21:04.020 --> 01:21:07.148
I love you, dear--

810
01:21:22.273 --> 01:21:25.367
From the gentleman.

811
01:21:37.521 --> 01:21:40.457
- You hate champagne.

812
01:21:40.525 --> 01:21:43.688
- You got a diving assignment.

813
01:21:43.762 --> 01:21:46.253
Brooklyn Navy Yard.
Stand by diver.

814
01:21:46.331 --> 01:21:49.300
Brooklyn? Brooklyn!

815
01:21:49.367 --> 01:21:53.064
Oh, baby, we can have dinner
like an old married couple.

816
01:21:53.138 --> 01:21:55.800
Oh, well, baby,
I didn't take the job.

817
01:21:55.874 --> 01:21:59.038
We've been waiting three years
for that slot to open up.

818
01:21:59.112 --> 01:22:01.580
Jo, I don't move up
in rank unless I dive.

819
01:22:01.647 --> 01:22:05.048
And I'll never make Master as a stand by
diver. I'll find something else.

820
01:22:11.824 --> 01:22:15.352
- I'm three months late.
- Late for what?

821
01:22:21.535 --> 01:22:25.164
You're gonna have--
A real... baby?

822
01:22:25.239 --> 01:22:29.005
We're gonna have a baby!
We're gonna have a real baby!

823
01:22:29.076 --> 01:22:31.203
We're gonna have a baby.

824
01:22:31.278 --> 01:22:34.145
Ladies, gentlemen,
and the rest of you lowdown cats,
it's time to ring in the New Year.

825
01:22:34.145 --> 01:22:35.976
Ladies, gentlemen,
and the rest of you lowdown cats,
it's time to ring in the New Year.

826
01:22:36.047 --> 01:22:41.314
- Happy New Year.
- Five, four, three, two, one.

827
01:22:41.385 --> 01:22:44.354
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year!

828
01:22:48.159 --> 01:22:50.650
You'll never know

829
01:22:50.728 --> 01:22:54.256
Just how much I love you

830
01:22:54.333 --> 01:22:58.565
Absolutely. You have to
stand them up, being we have
16, 20 years of experience.

831
01:22:58.637 --> 01:23:01.105
You have to get in their face
and let them know who's boss.

832
01:23:01.173 --> 01:23:03.903
If you don't, they'll never
salute you the rest of your life.

833
01:23:03.976 --> 01:23:06.604
So I'm sitting there--
Excuse me.

834
01:23:06.678 --> 01:23:11.116
- What'd I tell you, huh?
He don't remember me.

835
01:23:14.454 --> 01:23:18.823
Senior Chief Sunday,
U.S.S. Hoist.

836
01:23:18.891 --> 01:23:22.793
You ended my diving
career, Lieutenant.

837
01:23:22.862 --> 01:23:26.457
Lieutenant Commander Hanks.
Pleased to meet you.

838
01:23:26.532 --> 01:23:29.730
That was a long time ago, Chief.

839
01:23:29.803 --> 01:23:32.567
Ancient History.

840
01:23:32.639 --> 01:23:36.336
Well, we just came by
to say, "Hey."

841
01:23:36.410 --> 01:23:39.277
- Hey.
- Auld lang syne and all.

842
01:23:39.346 --> 01:23:43.476
Auld lang syne. I didn't
know you had a daughter.

843
01:23:43.550 --> 01:23:46.418
Right.

844
01:23:46.488 --> 01:23:48.456
She's quite lovely.

845
01:23:48.523 --> 01:23:53.358
Okay, we gotta gonow... because
Billy's gonna dance with me.

846
01:23:53.428 --> 01:23:55.521
Happy New Year.

847
01:23:55.597 --> 01:23:57.792
- Come on, Billy.
- Have fun.

848
01:23:57.866 --> 01:24:00.494
- You're gonna dance
with your lovely wife, right?
- Yeah.

849
01:24:07.109 --> 01:24:10.772
Mmm, you see?
Now, wasn't that easy?

850
01:24:10.846 --> 01:24:13.110
Has-been.

851
01:24:13.182 --> 01:24:18.779
- Yes.
- No. Billy.

852
01:24:18.854 --> 01:24:22.313
- He's the biggest drunk
in the Navy is all heis.
- Billy!

853
01:24:32.302 --> 01:24:35.100
Are you all right, sir?

854
01:24:38.108 --> 01:24:41.806
Senior Chief Sunday,
I find you guilty...

855
01:24:41.879 --> 01:24:44.905
of violating Article 90 of

856
01:24:44.982 --> 01:24:47.348
assaulting a superior
commissioned officer.

857
01:24:47.418 --> 01:24:50.251
Your conduct
is completely unacceptable.

858
01:24:50.321 --> 01:24:53.484
You'll be fined one half
month's pay for six months,

859
01:24:53.558 --> 01:24:56.618
restricted to the confines
of the base for two months...

860
01:24:56.694 --> 01:25:00.756
and are hereby reduced in rank
to Chief Petty Officer.

861
01:25:00.833 --> 01:25:01.467
For those just joining
us, our top story continues to unfold...

862
01:25:01.467 --> 01:25:04.300
For those just joining
us, our top story continues to unfold...

863
01:25:04.369 --> 01:25:07.395
thousands of miles away
in the Mediterranean Sea.

864
01:25:07.473 --> 01:25:10.203
Just hours ago,
an American B-52 bomber...

865
01:25:10.275 --> 01:25:13.005
flying a routine mission
over the coast of Spain...

866
01:25:13.078 --> 01:25:15.603
slammed into the snowy
Spanish countryside.

867
01:25:15.681 --> 01:25:20.085
Moments before disappearing off radar,
the crew jettisoned
their nuclear payload.

868
01:25:20.153 --> 01:25:22.678
Three 50-megaton warheads
parachuted to Earth.

869
01:25:22.755 --> 01:25:24.950
Two were immediately recovered.

870
01:25:25.024 --> 01:25:29.051
- However, a third hydrogen bomb
remains lost at sea.
- You made it.

871
01:25:29.129 --> 01:25:33.293
- United States Navyships have
sonar systems to aid them...
- Becky, come get your toys.

872
01:25:33.366 --> 01:25:36.803
in their tedious, often frustrating
search of the sea floor.

873
01:25:36.871 --> 01:25:39.863
Investigating a deep water find
will be the work of Alvin,

874
01:25:39.940 --> 01:25:44.138
a two-man submersible on loan from
the Woods Hole Oceanographic Institute.

875
01:25:44.211 --> 01:25:48.511
And yet, even as U.S. Navy ships
comb the Mediterranean
in search of the warhead,

876
01:25:48.582 --> 01:25:50.550
so do Russian submarines.

877
01:25:50.618 --> 01:25:54.020
According to maritime law,
the bomb which disappeared
in international waters...

878
01:25:54.089 --> 01:25:56.557
belongs to the first
to find it.

879
01:25:56.625 --> 01:25:59.651
Charged with locating and recovering
the lost bomb before the Soviets do...

880
01:25:59.728 --> 01:26:02.720
are the elite Navy deep-sea
divers pictured here.

881
01:26:02.797 --> 01:26:07.393
Stationed in Norfolk, Virginia,
the divers were flown by jet
to the scene just hours ago,

882
01:26:07.469 --> 01:26:11.201
many still dressedin the same uniforms
they were wearing only this morning.

883
01:26:22.185 --> 01:26:24.619
Blue Diver,
this is Captain.

884
01:26:28.357 --> 01:26:30.588
Blue Diver, come in.

885
01:26:30.661 --> 01:26:34.495
I'm here, Hart.
What do you need?

886
01:26:34.565 --> 01:26:37.728
Carl, I'd appreciate it if you
could find my lost nuke for me.

887
01:26:37.801 --> 01:26:40.326
I'd like to make admiral
sometime before Idie.

888
01:26:40.404 --> 01:26:43.032
I'm doing my best, Hart.

889
01:27:08.067 --> 01:27:10.592
Captain.

890
01:27:10.669 --> 01:27:14.264
Topside, I have an unidentified metal
object protruding from the sea bottom.

891
01:27:14.340 --> 01:27:16.672
He's got something.
Proceed with extreme caution.

892
01:27:16.742 --> 01:27:18.767
Roger that.

893
01:27:27.654 --> 01:27:30.020
Topside, we have a Coke can.

894
01:27:30.090 --> 01:27:32.581
Goddamn Coke can.

895
01:27:32.659 --> 01:27:35.753
Bring it on up anyway, Chief.
I like my ocean clean.

896
01:27:38.965 --> 01:27:43.300
- Turn that equipment off.
We got a diver down there.

897
01:27:43.371 --> 01:27:46.636
- That's not our sonar.
- What are you talking about?

898
01:27:46.707 --> 01:27:50.074
Shit.

899
01:27:50.144 --> 01:27:52.578
Alpha Whiskey,
this is Charlie Victor.

900
01:27:52.647 --> 01:27:56.674
I've got an unknown object
in my perimeter--
classified, probable submarine.

901
01:27:56.751 --> 01:28:01.052
Blue Diver, Blue Diver,
we got an unknown contact.
Probable Russian submarine...

902
01:28:01.123 --> 01:28:05.992
bearing at two-zero-niner
at sixteen knots and headed
directly for your position.

903
01:28:06.061 --> 01:28:09.519
Take immediate evasive action.
Repeat, immediate evasive action.

904
01:28:09.598 --> 01:28:14.194
Prepare for emergency surface.
Blue Diver, do you hear me?
Blue Diver, do you hear me?

905
01:28:14.269 --> 01:28:16.203
Blue Diver?

906
01:28:18.908 --> 01:28:21.240
Talk to me, Carl.

907
01:28:50.374 --> 01:28:53.572
Talk to me, Carl.

908
01:29:04.856 --> 01:29:06.983
Come in, Blue Diver.

909
01:29:16.202 --> 01:29:19.399
Quarter master, tell the dive station
to supply us a standby.

910
01:29:19.472 --> 01:29:21.406
Comein, Carl.

911
01:29:31.685 --> 01:29:34.654
Come on, Carl.

912
01:29:52.907 --> 01:29:56.775
- Carl, youread me?
- I'm here, Captain.

913
01:29:56.844 --> 01:29:59.210
He's there.

914
01:29:59.280 --> 01:30:03.546
- Prepare to surface, Carl.
We're bringing you home.
- Roger that.

915
01:30:11.693 --> 01:30:16.528
You wanna do me a favor?
The next time you scare me,
give me a courtesy warning first.

916
01:30:27.644 --> 01:30:30.841
Captain, that sub kicked up
half the ocean bottom.

917
01:30:30.914 --> 01:30:34.145
- It found it for us!
- You're kidding me.

918
01:30:34.217 --> 01:30:36.742
Oh, yeah!

919
01:30:36.820 --> 01:30:39.687
He thinks he found it.
Yeah, you got it.

920
01:30:39.756 --> 01:30:43.124
That's it. You got it.

921
01:30:43.194 --> 01:30:47.563
Steady! Steady!
I'm pulling it in!

922
01:30:47.631 --> 01:30:50.998
- Bring it up!
- Pull it up here, boys.

923
01:30:51.068 --> 01:30:54.526
Steady!
It's coming up toport.

924
01:30:54.605 --> 01:30:58.564
Let's go, boys! We got an A-bomb!

925
01:30:58.642 --> 01:31:01.407
It's coming up, boys!
Let's go now! Let's go, boys!

926
01:31:01.480 --> 01:31:05.271
We got a heavy one here.

927
01:31:16.482 --> 01:31:19.680
Move!

928
01:32:21.284 --> 01:32:23.252
Jo?

929
01:32:27.490 --> 01:32:31.450
Baby. Baby.

930
01:32:31.529 --> 01:32:34.498
I was so scared.

931
01:32:34.565 --> 01:32:37.398
I'm sorry.

932
01:32:43.174 --> 01:32:45.267
Oh, shit.

933
01:32:49.514 --> 01:32:52.915
Your leg...
was nearly severed.

934
01:32:56.288 --> 01:32:58.483
It's gonna take time to heal.

935
01:33:00.692 --> 01:33:04.924
Eventually, you're gonna be able
to walk again w-w-with a cane.

936
01:33:07.867 --> 01:33:10.165
Can I still dive?

937
01:33:12.638 --> 01:33:14.606
I'm so sorry.

938
01:33:50.645 --> 01:33:52.840
Come home, Carl.

939
01:34:00.488 --> 01:34:04.892
- Mrs. Sunday, your husband was
found drunk on a public beach.

940
01:34:04.960 --> 01:34:09.192
He's an alcoholic and must
remain in detox for 30 days.

941
01:34:09.265 --> 01:34:12.428
- If he should stagger,
he will not fall!

942
01:34:12.501 --> 01:34:15.800
If he should fall, he will
fall in such a manner...

943
01:34:15.871 --> 01:34:20.434
as to coverup his rate so that
passersby will think he's an officer.

944
01:34:23.380 --> 01:34:26.543
A chief petty officer
shall not drink!

945
01:34:26.616 --> 01:34:30.211
And if he should drink,
he shall not get drunk!

946
01:34:30.287 --> 01:34:34.018
If he should get drunk,
he shall not stagger!

947
01:34:34.090 --> 01:34:37.457
And if he should stagger,
he shall not fall!

948
01:34:37.527 --> 01:34:42.227
And if he should fall, he will fall in
such a manner as to cover up his rate...

949
01:34:42.300 --> 01:34:46.066
so that passersby
will think he's an officer!

950
01:34:46.137 --> 01:34:49.573
We're all extremely
proud of you, Chief Brashear.

951
01:34:49.640 --> 01:34:54.577
Now, get better, so you can go home
and enjoy your retirement.

952
01:34:54.645 --> 01:34:57.945
How do you plan to spend
your retirement, Chief Brashear?

953
01:34:58.016 --> 01:35:00.416
Howdoes it feel to be a hero?

954
01:35:20.473 --> 01:35:22.407
How are you?

955
01:36:02.117 --> 01:36:04.051
Sweetheart...

956
01:36:08.457 --> 01:36:10.687
you're never gonna dive again.

957
01:36:15.564 --> 01:36:18.465
And what you gotta do now...

958
01:36:18.534 --> 01:36:20.729
I can't help you with.

959
01:36:25.741 --> 01:36:27.835
But when you're
ready to leave...

960
01:36:27.911 --> 01:36:30.175
and if you can promise me...

961
01:36:30.247 --> 01:36:33.148
that you'll never
take another drink again,

962
01:36:33.216 --> 01:36:36.811
I'll be waiting for you
in that car over there.

963
01:36:39.923 --> 01:36:42.084
But if you can't...

964
01:36:48.599 --> 01:36:50.863
then you just walk on by.

965
01:37:34.380 --> 01:37:37.042
Package for you, sir.

966
01:38:00.308 --> 01:38:03.243
I want to comeback.

967
01:38:03.311 --> 01:38:05.376
- To where, Chief?
- Full diving duty.

968
01:38:05.376 --> 01:38:05.671
- To where, Chief?
- Full diving duty.

969
01:38:05.743 --> 01:38:08.234
I want to dive again.

970
01:38:08.312 --> 01:38:12.043
Carl, I understand, but, uh--

971
01:38:12.116 --> 01:38:15.109
But it's just not possible.

972
01:38:15.187 --> 01:38:19.817
- Good afternoon, Admiral.
- Carl, this is Cap--

973
01:38:19.891 --> 01:38:22.291
- Captain Hanks.
- Chief Brashear.

974
01:38:22.360 --> 01:38:25.727
Captain Hanks has been assigned
as a senior officer...

975
01:38:25.797 --> 01:38:29.255
at the Personnel Policy
Control Board at the Pentagon.

976
01:38:29.334 --> 01:38:31.495
He'll be joining us
for a few weeks,

977
01:38:31.570 --> 01:38:35.405
meeting some of the men
from the front lines,
getting a feel for their concerns.

978
01:38:35.474 --> 01:38:37.499
Yes, and to return
to the chief's primary concern.

979
01:38:37.577 --> 01:38:42.037
Working as a Navy diver
with one good leg and the other--

980
01:38:42.114 --> 01:38:44.844
I'm sorry.
It's just not possible.

981
01:38:44.917 --> 01:38:47.408
Cut it off.

982
01:38:49.722 --> 01:38:53.682
"Pilots injured in flying accidents have
requested amputation of injured limbs.

983
01:38:53.760 --> 01:38:57.093
Fitted with the right prosthesis,
several of them have returned
to active duty."

984
01:38:59.566 --> 01:39:04.629
Cut off my leg and assemble
a full medical review board
12 weeks from today.

985
01:39:04.705 --> 01:39:08.971
It is then that I will demonstrate that
I am fit to return to full diving duty.

986
01:39:09.042 --> 01:39:11.534
I want to make Master Chief.

987
01:39:13.414 --> 01:39:18.215
We admire your courage, Chief,
however misplaced it may be.

988
01:39:18.286 --> 01:39:22.279
Please excuse us.

989
01:39:30.799 --> 01:39:36.465
I am a doctor, Carl.
My opinion might mean something here.

990
01:39:39.775 --> 01:39:45.577
I guess not. How are you
gonna come back with one leg?

991
01:39:45.649 --> 01:39:49.050
I could barely read once.
I found a way.

992
01:39:49.119 --> 01:39:51.349
Yeah.

993
01:39:51.421 --> 01:39:54.447
I could put up with
the months at sea,

994
01:39:54.524 --> 01:39:58.426
the dangerous assignments that
you never said no to, but this--

995
01:39:58.495 --> 01:40:01.089
What do you want from me?

996
01:40:01.164 --> 01:40:05.864
Do you want me to come home,
mow the lawn, put a wheelchair ramp in?

997
01:40:05.936 --> 01:40:10.202
- How am I gonna look at my own son?
- Leave him out of this.

998
01:40:10.274 --> 01:40:14.711
You're not doing this for him or for me.
This is about you.

999
01:40:14.779 --> 01:40:17.270
It's always been about you.

1000
01:40:17.348 --> 01:40:21.250
Admit it, Carl.

1001
01:40:21.319 --> 01:40:24.153
At least give me that much.

1002
01:40:33.565 --> 01:40:36.295
Why are you doing this to me?

1003
01:40:40.907 --> 01:40:42.898
Answer me, goddamn it!

1004
01:40:42.975 --> 01:40:47.275
Or I'm walking out of here,
and I am not coming back.

1005
01:41:21.616 --> 01:41:23.641
I love you,Jo.

1006
01:43:44.399 --> 01:43:46.833
- Get away from me!

1007
01:43:46.902 --> 01:43:49.336
- Piece of shit!

1008
01:43:49.404 --> 01:43:51.895
- Cookie.

1009
01:43:51.973 --> 01:43:55.204
- Goddamn!

1010
01:43:55.277 --> 01:43:57.905
- Looks like I missed
one hell of a party.

1011
01:44:04.120 --> 01:44:08.079
- I've been all over. Trouble, mostly.

1012
01:44:08.157 --> 01:44:12.457
- Navy gave me this second-class
diving school in Little Creek.

1013
01:44:12.528 --> 01:44:14.621
Don't amount to shit.

1014
01:44:18.235 --> 01:44:20.169
I made some calls.

1015
01:44:22.105 --> 01:44:24.198
Come Friday,
that Captain Hanks--

1016
01:44:24.274 --> 01:44:27.641
he's gonna convene a medical review
board, and he's gonna retire you.

1017
01:44:29.913 --> 01:44:32.882
- He said I had four weeks.
- He lied, cookie.

1018
01:44:32.950 --> 01:44:36.546
He don't give a shit how many
one-legged push-ups you can do.

1019
01:44:36.621 --> 01:44:39.784
He'd trade you and me and every
other old sea dog in the Navy...

1020
01:44:39.857 --> 01:44:42.451
for one glass-eyed
electronics technician.

1021
01:44:42.527 --> 01:44:44.552
The man's gonna retire
your ass.

1022
01:44:44.629 --> 01:44:46.620
I got my leg back.
I ain't done yet.

1023
01:44:46.698 --> 01:44:50.225
You got a stump on a wooden stick and
no goddamn chance of beating Hanks, son.

1024
01:44:55.608 --> 01:44:58.406
All I ever wanted to do
was to make Master Diver.

1025
01:44:58.477 --> 01:45:01.913
All I ever wanted to do
was stay one.

1026
01:45:01.981 --> 01:45:07.351
You want to beat Hanks, you've got to
go around him, right to the top.

1027
01:45:07.419 --> 01:45:10.411
- Washington.
- Mm-hmm.

1028
01:45:10.489 --> 01:45:13.584
- Chief of Naval Personnel.
- That's right.

1029
01:45:13.660 --> 01:45:17.721
And they don't like cocky pencil-pushers
like Hanks any more than we do.

1030
01:45:20.667 --> 01:45:23.227
I might be able
to pull a few strings.

1031
01:45:29.977 --> 01:45:32.070
Why are you doing this,
Sunday?

1032
01:45:35.516 --> 01:45:37.450
Piss people off.

1033
01:45:37.518 --> 01:45:41.887
Chief Decker, you are the Chief Master
at Arms of this hospital, are you not?

1034
01:45:41.956 --> 01:45:44.584
Yes, sir.

1035
01:45:44.659 --> 01:45:49.597
Then why is it you don't know
where Chief Brashear is?

1036
01:45:49.665 --> 01:45:52.225
He shouldn't be
too hard to spot.

1037
01:45:52.301 --> 01:45:55.828
He is the only Negro
diver in the Navy,

1038
01:45:55.904 --> 01:45:57.895
and he's got one leg.

1039
01:45:57.973 --> 01:46:02.307
It seems that the chief
has transferred, sir.

1040
01:46:02.377 --> 01:46:04.709
To where?

1041
01:46:04.780 --> 01:46:08.273
- On whose orders?
- He signed his own orders, sir.

1042
01:46:08.351 --> 01:46:12.082
- Call the Shore Patrol.
- Relax, Cap. We just wanna talk.

1043
01:46:13.690 --> 01:46:17.649
Wait, wait, wait, wait. You know
where Chief Brashear is. Where?

1044
01:46:20.330 --> 01:46:23.766
I see. Fine.
Chief Brashear is AWOL.

1045
01:46:23.833 --> 01:46:25.995
I want him found
and arrested now.

1046
01:46:26.070 --> 01:46:30.131
- You ain't gonna find him.
- What doyou want from me, Chief?

1047
01:46:30.207 --> 01:46:33.108
Four weeks to train him, then
a full readiness evaluation...

1048
01:46:33.177 --> 01:46:35.907
and reinstatement hearing with
the Chief of Naval Personnel.

1049
01:46:35.979 --> 01:46:37.708
The chief of--

1050
01:46:37.781 --> 01:46:40.147
- Yes, sir.
- At the Navy yard in Washington?

1051
01:46:40.217 --> 01:46:42.082
- That's right.
- Forget it.

1052
01:46:47.359 --> 01:46:51.693
- Will the diver be allowed
to be reinstated?

1053
01:46:51.763 --> 01:46:56.632
Seems Chief Brashear
losing his leg for his country
sort of makes him a hero, sir.

1054
01:46:56.701 --> 01:46:58.635
Fine.

1055
01:47:03.242 --> 01:47:07.542
I will grant you your hearing
on one condition, hmm?

1056
01:47:07.613 --> 01:47:11.549
When he fails, you retire.

1057
01:47:11.617 --> 01:47:15.314
- He ain't gonna fail.
- Hmm.

1058
01:47:57.933 --> 01:48:00.458
Minute, five faster.

1059
01:48:04.506 --> 01:48:07.236
See you in court.

1060
01:49:42.523 --> 01:49:45.084
Captain Hanks has ordered you
to remain here, Chief.

1061
01:50:11.888 --> 01:50:14.254
Please be seated,
Senior Chief Brashear.

1062
01:50:20.030 --> 01:50:23.466
Um, only the Army
salutes indoors, Senior Chief.

1063
01:50:23.534 --> 01:50:26.799
Sir, in the Navy I grew up in,
a salute is warranted...

1064
01:50:26.871 --> 01:50:29.431
given the gravity
of this occasion, sir.

1065
01:50:29.507 --> 01:50:32.635
Well... we're in a new Navy now,
Senior Chief.

1066
01:50:37.681 --> 01:50:40.446
Shall we begin?

1067
01:50:41.620 --> 01:50:43.554
Senior Chief Brashear,

1068
01:50:43.622 --> 01:50:46.523
one day the life of another
diver may depend on you.

1069
01:50:46.591 --> 01:50:50.652
Do you honestly feel
that as a man--

1070
01:50:52.364 --> 01:50:56.096
You're almost 40.
You have one leg.

1071
01:50:56.169 --> 01:50:59.866
Can you really keep up with
healthy divers half your age?

1072
01:50:59.939 --> 01:51:04.501
The question is, sir,
can they keep up with me?

1073
01:51:07.113 --> 01:51:09.547
- Bring the suit.
- Yes, sir.

1074
01:51:11.050 --> 01:51:13.382
No smoking
out here, Chief.

1075
01:51:25.666 --> 01:51:30.194
Studies of
the Navy's experimental diving unit...

1076
01:51:30.270 --> 01:51:34.537
indicate that if the subject
were to become unconscious...

1077
01:51:34.609 --> 01:51:38.841
or deceased, the disparity
between the buoyancy characteristics...

1078
01:51:38.913 --> 01:51:43.714
of a prosthetic and a limb
would hinder him in a free dive mode.

1079
01:51:43.785 --> 01:51:47.516
You mean if he drowned,
he wouldn't float right, yes?

1080
01:51:47.589 --> 01:51:50.559
- Yes, sir.
- Sir, I promise,

1081
01:51:50.626 --> 01:51:55.120
if I am killed at sea, I will make
every effort to die like a Navy man.

1082
01:52:21.191 --> 01:52:24.319
I just thought you should see
the future of Navy deep sea diving.

1083
01:52:24.394 --> 01:52:26.989
This is the latest HEO-2
mixed gas rig.

1084
01:52:27.064 --> 01:52:29.897
It weighs 290 pounds,
and the men who want to use it,

1085
01:52:29.967 --> 01:52:32.492
before they can even begin
the diving qualifications,

1086
01:52:32.570 --> 01:52:35.903
will be required to walk
12 steps, unassisted.

1087
01:52:38.209 --> 01:52:41.269
Could you do that,
Senior Chief Brashear?

1088
01:52:48.387 --> 01:52:50.753
Yes, sir, I could.

1089
01:52:50.822 --> 01:52:53.518
Well... I see.

1090
01:52:53.592 --> 01:52:56.755
As much as I hate
to prolong this another day,

1091
01:52:56.828 --> 01:52:58.819
I will, in the interests
of thoroughness,

1092
01:52:58.897 --> 01:53:01.457
make arrangements for you
to demonstrate your contention.

1093
01:53:01.533 --> 01:53:04.435
Here, sir. Now.

1094
01:53:04.504 --> 01:53:08.440
Son, step aside, or I'll have to
crack you right in the jaw.

1095
01:53:11.244 --> 01:53:14.213
Senior Chief Brashear,
I hardly think this is the appropriate--

1096
01:53:14.280 --> 01:53:19.616
- I want them all to see, sir.
- Captain Hanks, sir,
I concur with your assessment.

1097
01:53:23.757 --> 01:53:27.056
These slippery floors alone prohibit
such a demonstration, sir.

1098
01:53:27.127 --> 01:53:31.860
Chief Sunday, haven't you had
enough trouble in your career?
Your advice is unwelcome.

1099
01:53:31.932 --> 01:53:35.197
- Who is this man?
- Chief Leslie W. Sunday, sir.

1100
01:53:35.269 --> 01:53:39.798
You swam out of the Saint Lo
at Leyte Gulf.

1101
01:53:41.409 --> 01:53:45.038
You held your breath
for four minutes.

1102
01:53:45.113 --> 01:53:47.206
Five, sir.

1103
01:53:48.817 --> 01:53:50.808
He can stay.

1104
01:53:53.254 --> 01:53:56.314
Fine. Irrelevant.

1105
01:53:56.391 --> 01:54:00.055
Gentlemen, sirs,
returning to the issue at hand.

1106
01:54:00.129 --> 01:54:04.190
This is not the time or place
for Senior Chief Brashear--

1107
01:54:06.335 --> 01:54:09.463
Excuse me, Senior Chief,
is there a problem?

1108
01:54:12.742 --> 01:54:18.613
Captain Hanks, I have spent most of my
life in the Navy trying only to succeed.

1109
01:54:18.682 --> 01:54:22.584
However, my questhas come at a great
personal loss to those who love me.

1110
01:54:22.653 --> 01:54:25.281
They, too,
have made sacrifices.

1111
01:54:25.355 --> 01:54:28.552
They, too, have endured
great pains to support me.

1112
01:54:28.625 --> 01:54:33.859
If I  walk these 12 steps today,
reinstate me to active duty.

1113
01:54:33.931 --> 01:54:35.956
Give me my career back.

1114
01:54:36.034 --> 01:54:40.130
Let me finish it
and go home in peace.

1115
01:54:42.707 --> 01:54:46.143
Senior Chief Brashear,
the business of the modern Navy--

1116
01:54:46.210 --> 01:54:50.237
Forgive me, sir. But to me,
the Navy is not a business.

1117
01:54:50.314 --> 01:54:54.251
We have many traditions. In my career,
I have experienced most of them.

1118
01:54:54.319 --> 01:54:56.913
Some good, some bad.

1119
01:54:56.989 --> 01:55:00.948
However, I wouldn't be here today
if it weren't for
our greatest tradition of all.

1120
01:55:01.026 --> 01:55:03.756
And which one is that?

1121
01:55:03.829 --> 01:55:06.559
Honor, sir.

1122
01:55:15.341 --> 01:55:18.242
Get on with it,
Senior Chief.

1123
01:55:20.914 --> 01:55:22.848
Leslie?

1124
01:55:24.584 --> 01:55:26.745
What leg you got on?

1125
01:55:26.820 --> 01:55:29.619
My walkin' leg, Leslie.

1126
01:55:29.690 --> 01:55:32.215
It was my dad's name.
You got a problem with that?

1127
01:55:32.293 --> 01:55:35.023
Oh, no.
No problem at all.

1128
01:55:40.835 --> 01:55:44.202
That thing's light duty.
Gonna snap like a match stick.

1129
01:55:44.271 --> 01:55:46.740
Not if I keep my weight
on my good leg.

1130
01:55:46.808 --> 01:55:50.869
Two hundred and ninety pounds
on one leg? You'll be
passed out by the sixth step.

1131
01:55:52.447 --> 01:55:55.416
Tenders, hat the diver.

1132
01:56:44.652 --> 01:56:46.643
Navy Diver, stand up.

1133
01:56:48.356 --> 01:56:50.483
Leave him.

1134
01:56:50.558 --> 01:56:54.085
Captain, if I recall the Navy
regulation manual correctly,

1135
01:56:54.161 --> 01:56:56.789
the diver
may be helped to his feet.

1136
01:56:56.864 --> 01:56:59.698
This is a lot of brass to sling up
from a seated position, sir.

1137
01:56:59.768 --> 01:57:03.636
It's spun copper, Chief.
We haven't used brass in a decade.

1138
01:57:03.705 --> 01:57:07.471
And the new manual states
the diver must rise unassisted.

1139
01:57:07.542 --> 01:57:11.137
That's what it says
in the new book, sir?

1140
01:57:11.213 --> 01:57:14.512
If I may ask, Captain,
how would you know?

1141
01:57:14.583 --> 01:57:16.346
I wrote it.

1142
01:57:19.289 --> 01:57:21.280
Yes, sir.

1143
01:57:27.230 --> 01:57:29.892
Navy Diver, stand up.

1144
01:57:39.476 --> 01:57:42.570
Square that rig
and approach the rail.

1145
01:58:03.034 --> 01:58:04.558
One.

1146
01:58:06.671 --> 01:58:08.070
Two.

1147
01:58:10.709 --> 01:58:12.234
Three.

1148
01:58:15.781 --> 01:58:17.271
Four.

1149
01:58:20.219 --> 01:58:21.652
Five.

1150
01:58:24.357 --> 01:58:25.756
Six.

1151
01:58:27.159 --> 01:58:28.456
Seven.

1152
01:58:29.997 --> 01:58:32.591
Eight.

1153
01:58:38.305 --> 01:58:40.773
Gentlemen, his leg.

1154
01:58:40.841 --> 01:58:43.776
Please. Gentlemen.

1155
01:58:46.313 --> 01:58:49.340
- Navy Diver, stand down.
- Diver, you will disregard.

1156
01:58:49.417 --> 01:58:52.250
- This is my detail.
- Admiral.

1157
01:58:52.320 --> 01:58:57.314
Goddamnit, cookie, move your ass!
I want my 12!

1158
01:59:09.271 --> 01:59:11.796
Nine. The Navy diver
is not a fighting man.

1159
01:59:11.874 --> 01:59:15.640
He is a salvage expert.
Ten.

1160
01:59:15.711 --> 01:59:19.306
If it's lost underwater, he finds it.
If it's sunk, he brings it up.

1161
01:59:19.381 --> 01:59:22.544
If it's in the way,
he moves it!

1162
01:59:22.618 --> 01:59:27.249
Eleven. If he's lucky, he will
die young 200 feet beneath the waves,

1163
01:59:27.323 --> 01:59:30.315
for that is the closest he will
ever get to being a hero!

1164
01:59:30.393 --> 01:59:33.726
Hell,I don't know why anybody
would want to be a Navy diver.

1165
01:59:33.797 --> 01:59:36.630
Now, you report
to this line, cookie!

1166
01:59:40.370 --> 01:59:43.397
At ease.

1167
01:59:54.218 --> 01:59:58.154
Tenders, unhat that diver.

1168
02:00:20.346 --> 02:00:23.509
The United States Navy
proudly reinstates...

1169
02:00:23.583 --> 02:00:27.713
Senior Chief and Diver
Carl Brashear...

1170
02:00:27.787 --> 02:00:30.620
to full, active duty.

1171
02:00:37.197 --> 02:00:39.688
Thank you.

1172
02:00:48.142 --> 02:00:50.576
Congratulations, Captain.

1173
02:00:50.644 --> 02:00:52.771
Thank you.

1174
02:01:06.494 --> 02:01:08.394
I can quit.

1175
02:01:08.463 --> 02:01:12.059
The man I married never quit
anything a day in his life.

1176
02:01:17.106 --> 02:01:19.040
I love you.

1177
02:01:19.108 --> 02:01:23.408
I love you too, baby.
I love you too.

1178
02:01:39.229 --> 02:01:41.663
Well done, Chief.
